consistent with the paired 1.68 ms difference (4.1747-3.6787)/128 per token.

## Dominant-term gate (unmodified tree, f32)

  $ env APEIRON_THREADS=8 APEIRON_KV_CARRIER=f32 phase_split --model ... --pack ... \
      --steps 32 --prefix 1795 --target ffn
  | ffn | 6.286 | 23.0% | 896 |
  | attn.core | 12.198 | 44.6% | 896 |
  REFUSED: target ffn holds 23.0% (ceiling 1.30x); the dominant term is attn.core at 44.6%
  (ceiling 1.81x). Target the dominant term, or instrument it if it is the untraced remainder.
  exit 1

target `ffn` is not the dominant term, so the gate refuses: this change is a kernel step on the
rank-stage reader, not a campaign speedup. The next lever is attn.core (44.6%, ceiling 1.81x).

