## Assembly note

`code_select_avx2` (per-row entry) is one serial 5-op select chain per 32-term block with a
`call` and seven `push`es per output row; `code_select_block_avx2` (the reader behind
`Stage::dot_rows`) hoists the code load, the shift load and the selector constants once per block
and gives each row its own accumulator chain. `/tmp/llvm/ours-decode.s` on the box holds the
disassembly; the blocked entry is `code_select_block_avx2::<8>`.
